    "updated_at": "2026-11-10T17:18:26Z",
    "body": "GPU evidence from a machine that has a real adapter - the review ran headless, so the `gpu`-gated suites here close that gap.\n\n**Machine:** Windows laptop, two adapters enumerated - `NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 Ti Laptop GPU` (the one picked, via `dx12`) and the Intel Iris Xe integrated part.\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib gpu` | 24 passed, 0 failed |\n| `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --test gpu_render` | 10 passed, 0 failed |\n\nThe integration suite includes the pin for this fix:\n\n```\ntest orthographic_paints_the_band_perspective_does ... ok\n```\n\nBoth run at `f5181677` - my open #645 branch tip, which is `origin/main` (`ed24aead`) merged in, so it carries the shipped #604 code plus that PR's comment-only changes.\n\n**By hand in the running app** (`cargo run -p camcraft-ui`): the orthographic toggle was driven through the live GPU path and confirmed visually - the view changes projection and renders cleanly. The app's own log line reads `NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 Ti Laptop GPU via dx12`, so this is the real adapter path, not a software fallback.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
